<title>BELGIUM: BELGIUM ASKS SIEMENS AND THOMSON FOR MILITARY BID.</title>
<headline>BELGIUM ASKS SIEMENS AND THOMSON FOR MILITARY BID.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government on Friday agreed to ask Germany's Siemens and Thomson CSF of France to bid to supply the army with a one billion franc information command and control system.</p>
<p>The first segment of the contract will be worth 700 million Belgian francs and the second 300 million. There will then be a 20 million franc annual maintenance contract.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
